## Events sent to things, which every target must deliver alike

a "card" is a thing where:
	- its "name" is text
	- its "flips" is a number
	- its "locked" is a choice
	- it sends "flipped" with side as a text

	- to create it:
		set its flips to 0

	- to flip it:
		set its flips to its flips + 1
		send flipped with side = "up"
		print "[its name] flipped"

	// taken here:  its pile never hears it
	- when flipped with side as text:
		print "[its name] heard flipped [side]"

	// handed on up:  its pile hears it too
	- when picked:
		print "[its name] heard picked"
		pass event

	- when its flips changes:
		print "[its name] has flipped [its flips] times"

	// a handler that waits:  what sends it waits for it
	- when slowly flipped:
		pause for 10 msec
		print "[its name] slowly flipped"

	- to flip it slowly:
		send slowly flipped
		print "[its name] done slowly"

	// an event still happening can be canceled:  the step after it doesn't run
	- to close it:
		send closing
		print "[its name] closed"

	- when closing:
		if its locked:
			print "[its name] won't close"
			cancel event


a "pile" is a list of cards where:
	- when picked:
		print "the pile heard picked"
		pass event

	- when flipped with side as text:
		print "the pile heard flipped"

a card belongs to one pile

on picked:
	print "the program heard picked"

on lonely:
	print "the program heard lonely"

to play the story:
	get a new pile
	set the pile to it
	get a new card with name = "ace"
	set the ace to it
	add it to the pile
	get a new card with name = "king", locked = yes
	set the king to it

	close the ace
	close the king
	send picked to the ace
	send lonely to the ace
	send nobody listens to the ace
	flip the ace
	flip the ace slowly
	print "the end"

play the story
